  "goodToKnow": "Das Unkraut is weeds, a collective noun: Unkraut jäten (to weed), Unkrautvernichtungsmittel (weedkiller). Gardeners now prefer the more neutral Wildkraut. Unkraut vergeht nicht (weeds never die) is said jokingly about someone resilient, often oneself after illness. Das Kraut means herb or plant, and in the south, cabbage: Sauerkraut. Glyphosate, a common weedkiller, is debated in Germany. It has no plural."
